# Compose defaults for `docker compose up --build`, read automatically from the
# project directory. Variables set in the shell take precedence, which is how a
# caller points the facade at another backend (no stand-in, so no state reset):
#   COMPOSE_PROFILES= BACKEND_REST_URL=http://<host>:65000 BACKEND_SOAP_URL=http://<host>:21001 BACKEND_ADMIN_URL= docker compose up --build
# Ports 65000 and 21001 are those of the ErewhonREST and WebServiceHTTP
# applications in Erewhon/ErehwhonExternalInterfacesSchema.ddx, both plain HTTP.
# 9090 is the stand-in's unpublished admin port (AdminRoutes.DefaultPort), and
# BACKEND_TIMEOUT_SECONDS is the facade's deadline for each backend call.
# Backends are addressed by URL only; no Windows install path appears here.
COMPOSE_PROFILES=standin
BACKEND_REST_URL=http://standin:65000
BACKEND_SOAP_URL=http://standin:21001
BACKEND_ADMIN_URL=http://standin:9090
BACKEND_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=30
